Subject: [PATCH 3/3] [3.1.4][E: 8078 post-.109] [M156] GL: Reset base level for ASTC robust init

Original change's description:
> GL: Reset base level for ASTC robust init
>
> On PowerVR GPUs, calling glCompressedTexSubImage2D on ASTC textures
> with TEXTURE_BASE_LEVEL > 0 causes an out-of-bounds CPU write in
> TwiddleSmallTexture128bpp.
>
> While resetBaseLevelForASTCImage handled setCompressedImage and
> setCompressedSubImage, it was missing in initializeContentsImpl
> (for robust resource initialization), setImageViaScratchUnpackBuffer,
> and the setStorage fallback loops.
>
> In WebGL, robust resource initialization uploads zero data via
> compressedTexSubImage2D before drawing. If TEXTURE_BASE_LEVEL was set
> to a non-zero value, this caused the PowerVR driver to crash during
> draw calls.
>
> Bug: b/562857750
> Test: angle_end2end_tests --gtest_filter="*ASTCCompressed*"
> Change-Id: I2b5a4e4c6e8a4e197b8f935075f4acb55b13c775
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8422465
> Reviewed-by: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>
> Commit-Queue: Tzarial <zork@chromium.org>
> Reviewed-by: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>

